<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                   http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.20.xsd"
                   logicalFilePath="config/liquibase/changelog/platform/knowledge_base/20260901000002_platform_knowledge_base_document_source_record_owner.xml">

    <!--
        uk_kb_doc_source_record made (source_id, source_record_id) unique on the premise that a source record has one
        document. Row-level ownership made that false: two accounts may sync one shared source into one shared
        knowledge base, and each account's copy of a record is its own document, carrying its own owner and its own
        chunks. The lookup that finds a document to rewrite is scoped by owner for that reason, so without this the
        second account's run would find nothing and then fail to insert.

        Two partial indexes rather than one on four columns. A single index over (source_id, source_record_id,
        owner_id, owner_type) enforces nothing for the vendor's rows: Postgres treats every NULL as distinct, so two
        unowned documents of the same source record would both insert.

        The predicates are complementary and cover every row with a source_id, so no row escapes both. A document
        carrying an owner_id beside a null owner_type belongs to nobody, and the unowned index is deliberately the one
        that claims it, which is the same answer the read and write predicates give that shape.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260901000002-1" author="Ivica Cardic">
        <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS uk_kb_doc_source_record;</sql>
        <sql>CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uk_kb_doc_source_record_owned ON knowledge_base_document (source_id, source_record_id, owner_id, owner_type) WHERE source_id IS NOT NULL AND owner_id IS NOT NULL AND owner_type IS NOT NULL;</sql>
        <sql>CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uk_kb_doc_source_record_unowned ON knowledge_base_document (source_id, source_record_id) WHERE source_id IS NOT NULL AND (owner_id IS NULL OR owner_type IS NULL);</sql>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
